    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in the middle infield: **Gunnar Henderson** (81.00) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) are our undeniable anchors. Both benefit from a high-efficiency matchup against Cavalli and Bassitt, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s score is buoyed by a substantial +14% platoon advantage, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** mirrors that efficiency, cementing them as the engines of the lineup. In the outfield, **Sam Antonacci** (63.68) remains a high-upside play against Taillon, leveraging a top-tier xwOBA of 0.402, while **Heliot Ramos** (65.50) is the dark horse of the day; his score is significantly elevated by a +15% SP skill boost and a favorable +10% park factor against Severino, proving his worth as a strong start despite the volatile nature of the matchup.\n\nThe most challenging decision for the staff was the final bench spot, where **Nolan Schanuel** (45.00) nearly cracked the rotation. Ultimately, the optimizer prioritized the higher floors provided by **Liam Hicks** and **Drake Baldwin** in the catcher slots, as the scarcity of plate appearances necessitates maximizing those positions. We are tracking several \"Lineup Pending\" statuses closely, specifically for **Jackson Merrill**, **Josh Jung**, **Andy Pages**, and **Kyle Tucker**. While **Kyle Tucker** (63.54) carries a strong projection, we must remain vigilant regarding the confirmed order; should his lineup placement drop, his efficiency score will be subject to immediate downward revision. \n\nFinally, a note on risk: **Jackson Merrill** faces an elite arm in Gilbert (2.98 xERA), resulting in a significant -19% SP skill penalty that drags his score down to 52.77. While he remains a start, we are monitoring the wind and confirmation of his #1 slot to ensure he isn't neutralized. Our depth remains robust, though we are obviously missing the upside of **Luis Robert Jr.** on the IL, leaving the burden of speed-category production on our active core. We will keep **Coby Mayo** and **Josh Lowe** on high alert should any late-inning substitutions or weather delays force a mid-day pivot.",
